      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sudden, brief spikes often point toward sensor calibration issues or temporary power fluctuations affecting the monitoring system rather than a catastrophic compressor failure. It could also indicate a momentary blockage or control board hesitation within the refrigeration unit's electronic controls. Having a technician thoroughly test the sensor accuracy against an independent, calibrated thermometer is the best next step to distinguish between a reading error and an actual cooling malfunction.",
      "source": "target",
