      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the hardware appears perfect, the issue could be intermittent software bugs in the controller's programming or electromagnetic interference nearby disrupting the sensitive electronics. Sometimes, even minor fluctuations in external power supply quality can cause the control unit to momentarily misread or respond erratically. Given the unexplained nature, logging continuous, high-frequency data from multiple sensors might be necessary to capture the exact moment of the \"glitch.\"",
      "source": "target",
